# Host-specific runtime state, not project configuration.
# Records each kind node container's pinned IP so session-start.sh can
# restore it after a host/WSL restart. See scripts/session-start.sh.
clusters/kind/.node-ips
.claude/

# Gradle. Local cache/metadata and build output, regenerated from source
# every time, not something to track. The wrapper itself,
# apps/gradlew, apps/gradlew.bat,
# apps/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.{jar,properties}, is a different,
# non-dot-prefixed path and stays committed on purpose, that's the one
# artifact meant to be reproducible across machines.
#
# The whole Gradle build lives under apps/ so the repo root separates the
# Java build from the infrastructure (manifests/, clusters/, scripts/).
# The patterns below are path-agnostic, so they match apps/*/build/ too.
.gradle/
build/

# IDE. IntelliJ writes apps/.idea/ because the Gradle build root is apps/,
# not the repo root. Its contents are host-specific: gradleJvm points at an
# absolute JDK path, and the module classpath is external-storage state
# regenerated by a Gradle sync. Nothing here is reproducible on another
# machine, so none of it is shared.
.idea/
*.iml

# Third-party Helm chart, unpacked for reading only.
charts/
